From: Try Omarchy contributors
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: forward trackpad scrolling as touchpad finger scrolling

Applies after the pinch-zoom and precise-scroll patches. Precise,
non-momentum scrolling in the focused guest view drives two contacts on the
pinch touchpad, so libinput reports finger scrolling and Linux applications
can recognize swipe navigation. The gesture follows AppKit's scroll phases
and the pinch bridge's release rules. Momentum scrolling, discrete mouse
wheels and scrolling outside the focused view keep the tablet's wheel path.
The touchpad grows to an 800 mm sensor so one contact can carry a whole
swipe; pinch geometry keeps its size in millimetres. The touchpad also
advertises BTN_TOOL_TRIPLETAP.

